lwc trap that burns points:

the exam won't ask what @wire means.

it asks which decorator fits the scenario.

@wire = pull from salesforce
@api = value from parent
@track = reactive local state

know the job each one is hired for.

if you're brand new to Salesforce:

Admin. full stop.

Every other cert assumes you know profiles, OWD, validation rules. Skipping Admin is like skipping grammar to study literature — it just takes twice as long.

if i were starting today:

get the admin cert. then stop cert-stacking like a junkie and go build something real for a food bank before you touch another exam.

then get one specialist cert matching the exact job you want. that's the whole playbook.
